## 1. Purpose

This Open Questions Log tracks unresolved product, data, legal, technical, and sequencing questions that affect implementation readiness. Questions that are resolved should remain in the log for traceability but must point to the decision record or artifact that now governs the answer.

## 2. Recently Resolved Questions

The following questions were open during the duration/lead-time and sequencing review and are now resolved by **Decisions Log V11**.

| Question ID | Question | Resolution | Decision Reference | Status | Downstream Artifact Impact |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| OQ-SEQ-001 | Should **Accessibility improvements** be split into subtypes, or should the product use one conservative range covering the common case? | Split into subtypes. MVP should distinguish minor accessibility improvements, such as grab bars and threshold-level modifications, from larger exterior access modifications, such as ramps or access-path changes. | D-V11-001 | Resolved | Recommendation catalog, duration/lead-time seed table, dependency rules, Technical Specification V3 |
| OQ-SEQ-002 | Should **Professional staging** trigger an anomaly callout when staging is in the plan and the target list date is less than 21 days away? | Yes. If professional staging is recommended and the target list date is fewer than 21 calendar days away, the engine should trigger a staging timeline-risk anomaly. | D-V11-002 | Resolved | Recommendation anomaly rules, duration/lead-time rules, report-output logic, Technical Specification V3 |

## 3. Current Open Questions

The following questions remain open and should be resolved before implementation reaches the affected subsystem.

| Question ID | Question | Why It Matters | Recommended Owner / Reviewer | Required Before | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
